`ifndef CRG_RDL
`define CRG_RDL

regfile ePERI_CRG {
    name = "Clock and reset generator (CRG), Hi3519 V101";
    desc = "    PERI_CRGn clock/reset registers at 0x12010000 (CRG; `PERI_CRG` is the HiSilicon register prefix, offset = n x 4). Data sheet: Hi3519 V101 Professional HD IP Camera SoC, Issue 01 (2018-07-05), chapter 3.2 (Clock) and 3.1 (Reset), registers in 3.2.6/3.2.7; the Hi3516A V200 data sheet has the same CRG chapter, register for register (checked 2026-11-10: the same 43 registers, offsets, reset values and field tables; the only difference is PERI_CRG19 vedu_clksel, which lists 500 and 594 MHz codes only here). 43 registers, offsets 0x0-0x24 (PLLs), 0x28-0xF0 and 0x13C.

    Clock tree facts for bring-up. Input clocks: XIN = 24 MHz crystal, RTC_XIN = 32.768 kHz. Four PLLs, each with two configuration registers (DS Table 3-3): APLL = PERI_CRG_PLL0/1 (offsets 0x0/0x4), DPLL = PERI_CRG_PLL4/5 (0x10/0x14), VPLL = PERI_CRG_PLL6/7 (0x18/0x1C), EPLL = PERI_CRG_PLL8/9 (0x20/0x24). Formula (DS Table 3-4): FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv, which must stay above 800 MHz and at most 2.3 GHz; FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2) with postdiv1 >= postdiv2; FOUTVCO2X = 2 x FOUTVCO; FOUT1PH0/2/3/4 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8). Reset configurations: APLL 1200 MHz (refdiv 1, fbdiv 50, postdiv 2 x 1 = 600 MHz), DPLL 932 MHz (refdiv 6, fbdiv 233, POSTDIV 466 MHz), VPLL 1188 MHz (POSTDIV 594 MHz), EPLL 1500 MHz (POSTDIV 500 MHz); only the APLL and DPLL are meant to be reprogrammed (the VPLL and EPLL are fixed). PLL change procedure (DS 3.2.5.3): first switch every consumer of the PLL to a non-PLL (or another PLL) clock, change the PLL configuration, wait 0.1 ms and poll the lock bits PERI_CRG58[4:0] (apll [0], dpll [2], vpll [3], epll [4]; gzip_rst_ok is bit 8), then switch back once the PLL is locked.

    Clock muxes (DS 3.2.5, Tables 3-5/3-6; everything that has a mux resets to its first entry, normally the 24 MHz crystal): a7_clksel PERI_CRG13[9:7], a17_clksel PERI_CRG13[6:4], ddr_clksel PERI_CRG13[2:0], sysaxi_clksel PERI_CRG13[13:12] (completion indicators in PERI_CRG79); VDP: vdp_core_clksel PERI_CRG17[17], vdp_out_clksel [16:14], hd_div_mode [13:12], lcd_mclk_div PERI_CRG18[26:0]; sensor0/1_clksel PERI_CRG16[3:0]/[11:8]; vi0_clksel PERI_CRG19[2:0], vi1_clksel PERI_CRG21[2:0], isp0_clksel PERI_CRG21[18:14], isp1_clksel PERI_CRG21[10:6]; vedu/vpss/vgs/ive/gdc_clksel PERI_CRG19[12:10]/[7:5]/[15:13]/[21:19]/[18:16]; FMC fmc_clksel PERI_CRG48[4:2] (0: 24 MHz, 1: 75, 2: 125, 3: 150, 4: 198(200), 5: 250, 6: 300, 7: 396(400) MHz, confirmed by the vendor U-Boot platform.h and the vendor Linux clk-hi3519.c fmc_mux at 0xC0 [4:2], gate at bit 1); MMC mmc0/1/2_clksel PERI_CRG49[12:10]/[4:2]/[20:18] and mmc*_clk_mode [13]/[5]/[21] (must be 1); cipher ca_clksel PERI_CRG31[6]; PWM pwm_clksel PERI_CRG55[3:2] (3 MHz / 50 MHz / 24 MHz); UART uart_clksel PERI_CRG57[25] (1: 24 MHz; the vendor U-Boot sets it in board_init) and I2C i2c_clksel PERI_CRG57[26] (1: 50 MHz); GMAC mac_speed/port_select PERI_CRG59[1:0], ext_fephy_clksel PERI_CRG51[6], rmii_clksel PERI_CRG51[4]; AIAO aiao_clksel PERI_CRG32[3:2] (1188 MHz VPLL VCO or 1500 MHz EPLL VCO); USB: combphy_refclk_sel PERI_CRG43[9], usb3_utmi_clksel PERI_CRG46[13] (USB 2.0 controller and PHY in PERI_CRG45).

    Reset polarity: every *_srst_req bit is 1 = reset asserted, 0 = reset released (`0: reset deasserted, 1: reset`); *_clken bits are 1 = clock on. Several modules come up held in reset (srst_req resets to 1 for the A17 cluster, VEDU, VPSS, VDP, VI0, MIPI0, ISP0, USB, COMB PHY), so software must release them and enable the clock.

    Cross-checks: the vendor U-Boot 2010.06 (`arch-hi3519v101/platform.h` PERI_CRG43 = 0xAC, PERI_CRG57 = 0xE4, REG_CRG48 = 0xC0 for the FMC, REG_ETH_CRG = 0xCC = PERI_CRG51; `board/hi3519v101/board.c`) and the vendor-derived Linux clock driver (`drivers/clk/hisilicon/clk-hi3519.c`: fmc mux at 0xC0 bits [4:2] with the straight table 0..7, fmc gate 0xC0 bit 1, UART0-4 gates 0xE4 bits 20..24, SPI0-2 gates bits 16..18) use the same offsets and bits as this data sheet. The vendor code does not touch the a7/a17/ddr/sysaxi muxes (the boot ROM and the DDR training code set them), so the PERI_CRG13 value tables rest on the data sheet bit rows alone.

    Known data sheet errors and decisions (dump `hi3519v101--Hi3519V101-Datasheet.txt`, checked 2026-11-10): (1) PERI_CRG22 (VPSS) prints `Offset Address 0x0048` in its description block; the summary table and the register sequence put it at 0x58 (PERI_CRG18, the LCD register, owns 0x48): 0x58 is used. (2) PERI_CRG17 header reset 0x4 vs rows 0x5 (vdp_srst_req resets to 1) and PERI_CRG49 header 0x00020200 vs rows 0x00020202 (mmc1_clken resets to 1): the row values are used, low confidence. (3) For PERI_CRG10, 11, 15, 45, 54 the header total reset value has bits set that the rows call reserved: they are modelled as RO reserved_nz_<hi>_<lo> fields so that the register reset equals the header value. (4) DS Table 3-2 lists the A7/A17 frequency choices in the opposite order of the PERI_CRG13 rows (see the PERI_CRG13 register); the rows are followed. (5) PERI_CRG58 is RO (lock status) and PERI_CRG79 is RO (clock switch completion). (6) The previous RDL carried a placeholder `PERI_CRG68 @ 0x0110` (marked UNDOCUMENTED): it is not in the data sheet, not used by the vendor U-Boot nor by the OpenIPC clock driver, and has been dropped. (7) Field tables of PERI_CRG57 (test_clk_en, i2c_clksel and the lower reset bits) and several descriptions are mangled by the PDF layout; the meaning is taken from the bit table.

    Sources: HiSilicon's own English data sheet `Hi3519V101-Datasheet.pdf` (not machine translated; no watermark); no Chinese original available for this chip. Registers, fields and reset values were extracted from the text dump `hi3519v101--Hi3519V101-Datasheet.txt` (CRG register summary and description from 3.2.6/3.2.7) and compared programmatically with this file.
    ";

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 0";
        desc = "PERI_CRG_PLL0 is APLL configuration register 0.

APLL configuration register 0 (APLL = PERI_CRG_PLL0/PERI_CRG_PLL1). FOUTVCO = 24 MHz x (fbdiv + frac/2^24) / refdiv, must be above 800 MHz and at most 2.3 GHz (DS Table 3-4); FOUTPOSTDIV = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2) with postdiv1 >= postdiv2. Reset: postdiv2 = 1, postdiv1 = 2; with PERI_CRG_PLL1 (refdiv 1, fbdiv 50) FOUTVCO = 1200 MHz and POSTDIV = 600 MHz, which is also the worked example of DS 3.2.4. Change procedure: DS 3.2.5.3 (switch the consumers away first, reprogram, wait 0.1 ms, poll PERI_CRG58[4:0]).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG_PLL0 (offset 0x0, printed page 3-13, `hi3519v101--Hi3519V101-Datasheet.txt` line 4533).";

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv2";
            desc = "Level-2 output frequency divider of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_postdiv2[30:28];

        field {
            name = "apll_postdiv1";
            desc = "Level-1 output frequency divider of the APLL";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x2;
        } apll_postdiv1[26:24];

        field {
            name = "apll_frac";
            desc = "Decimal part of the APLL frequency multiplication coefficient";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_frac[23:0];
    } PERI_CRG_PLL0 @ 0x0;

    reg {
        name = "APLL configuration register 1";
        desc = "PERI_CRG_PLL1 is APLL configuration register 1.

APLL configuration register 1. Reset 0x09101032: foutvco2xpd 1, dsmpd 1 (integer mode, apll_frac ignored), fout4phasepd 1, refdiv 1, fbdiv 50. FOUTVCO2X = 2 x FOUTVCO; the phase outputs FOUT1PH0/2/3/4 = FOUTVCO / (postdiv1 x postdiv2 x 2/4/6/8).

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG_PLL1 (offset 0x4, printed page 3-14, `hi3519v101--Hi3519V101-Datasheet.txt` line 4572).";

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_foutvco2xpd_enum {
            NORMAL_OUTPUT = 0 { name = "Normal Output"; desc = "normal output clock"; };
            NO_OUTPUT = 1 { name = "No Output"; desc = "no output clock"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_foutvco2xpd";
            desc = "APLL VCO2X output power-down control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_foutvco2xpd_enum;
            reset = 0x1;
        } apll_foutvco2xpd[27:27];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_bypass_enum {
            NOT_BYPASSED = 0 { name = "Not Bypassed"; desc = "not bypassed"; };
            BYPASSED = 1 { name = "Bypassed"; desc = "bypassed"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_bypass";
            desc = "APLL clock frequency division bypass";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
            encode = PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_bypass_enum;
            reset = 0x0;
        } apll_bypass[26:26];

        enum PERI_CRG_PLL1_apll_dacpd_enum {
            NORMAL_OPERATING_MODE = 0 { name = "Normal Operating Mode"; desc = "normal operating mode"; };
            POWER_DOWN_MODE = 1 { name = "Power Down Mode"; desc = "power-down mode"; };
        };

        field {
            name = "apll_dacpd";
            desc = "APLL test signal control";
            sw = rw;
            hw = r;
