    reg {
        name = "Clock soft reset control register for other APB modules";
        desc = "PERI_CRG57 is a clock soft reset control register for other APB modules.

Clock gates, clock selects and soft resets of the low-speed APB peripherals (UART0-4 gates [24:20], SSP0-3, IR, I2C0-3 and T_CAP resets, PMC reset). uart_clksel [25] (0: SYS APB clock, 1: 24 MHz, reset 1) and i2c_clksel [26] (0: SYS APB clock, 1: 50 MHz, reset 1); the vendor U-Boot (platform.h PERI_CRG57 = 0xE4, UART_CKSEL_24M = 1 << 25, board.c board_init) sets bit 25, and the vendor Linux clk-hi3519.c gates are at 0xE4 bits 16..24 (SPI0-2 on bits 16-18, UART0-4 on bits 20-24), as in the data sheet. Reset 0x0E10_0000 = uart_clksel, i2c_clksel, test_clk_en and uart0_clken set. The data sheet text of bit 27/26 and of bits 3:0 is mangled by the PDF layout; names and meaning are taken from the bit table.

Data sheet 3.2.7 PERI_CRG57 (offset 0xE4, printed page 3-53, `hi3519v101--Hi3519V101-Datasheet.txt` line 6731).";

